+   "body": "<<passages (unscreened): HB-55 §1, HB-55 §2, HB-55 §3>>\n--- HB-55 §1 | Memo: relocation lump sum exceptions — Purpose | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-05-01\nThis memo lists group exceptions to the relocation lump sum in HB-34. Managers confirm claims for the relocation lump sum before payment in the next payroll run. The HR publishes worked examples of the relocation lump sum on the intranet.\n--- HB-55 §2 | Memo: relocation lump sum exceptions — Exception for relocations to another country | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-05-01\nFor relocations to another country, the relocation lump sum is 5000 EUR instead of the standard amount. The HR publishes worked examples of the relocation lump sum on the intranet. Each claim for the relocation lump sum needs a receipt showing the date, the amount and the supplier.\n--- HB-55 §3 | Memo: relocation lump sum exceptions — Carve-out | version: 1 · status: current · effective: 2025-05-01\nThe exception above does not apply to relocations within the first six months of employment; they follow the standard relocation lump sum in HB-34 §2. The HR reviews the relocation lump sum once a year and announces changes in advance. Claims for the relocation lump sum are filed in the expense tool under 'HR policy: relocation support'.\n<<end passages>>\n"
